WEBVTT

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.129
Another crossing burned.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.632
We might never reach Tumbleton.

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:15.010
So how long will it take you to build the bloody thing again?

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.387
We will have to find another crossing,

00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:20.974
- take the long way round. - The queen will abhor this delay.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.685
Lord Piper, take 100 of your fastest riders

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:26.145
And make for Stoney Sept.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.606
Secure the barge and transit there.

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:31.984
That puts us back by a week, but we can do no better.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:35.530
It's our last chance to ford the river with an army of this size.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.166
Will we continue to suffer this Cole

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.669
And his band of hangers-on?

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.797
They flit about us like fucking deer flies,

00:02:52.798 --> 00:02:55.841
Another thing that we do not endure in the North.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.552
Better deer flies than frostbite.

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:02.807
But Criston Cole I am past enduring, North or South.

00:03:02.808 --> 00:03:08.397
Then loose my wolves and me on the hunt, and we will bring him down.

00:03:09.815 --> 00:03:11.400
Or we could play at his game.

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:49.312
Ambush!

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:56.486
We're under attack!

00:04:00.741 --> 00:04:02.199
To the next crossing, then?

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.786
They'll make for Stoney Sept and we'll once more be ahead of them.

00:04:05.787 --> 00:04:07.164
Fall back!

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.452
If I'd have known we were expecting guests,

00:04:46.453 --> 00:04:48.204
I would have made up the beds.

00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:49.830
We're looking for Aemond Targaryen,

00:04:49.831 --> 00:04:52.291
- the Kinslayer. - Ah, yes. There's been a horde of you

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:55.962
Since the ungrateful queen announced her bounty.

00:04:56.797 --> 00:04:59.423
Well, you won't find your quarry here.

00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:04.137
There's an old man who churns the butter, but he's blind in both eyes.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.224
And the boy who feeds the horses.

00:05:08.266 --> 00:05:10.768
And then there are the ghosts.

00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:14.146
Seems you have not learned the history of this place

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:16.191
And the laborers who built it...

00:05:18.026 --> 00:05:20.862
Who died here in chains...

00:05:21.822 --> 00:05:23.406
In service to Harren the Cruel.

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:30.163
This castle breathes.

00:05:35.627 --> 00:05:39.214
She swallows the greedy, the heedless.

00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:45.971
Her founding stones were watered with the blood of men.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.975
And she's always thirsty.

00:06:08.577 --> 00:06:10.078
Oi! You bloody craven?!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.832
Fuck this place.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.682
Can you hear me?

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.394
Stay back! Stay back!

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.106
My brother. Aegon, he was here.

00:06:39.107 --> 00:06:40.859
His face was on fire.

00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:46.238
I saw him. He was clutching at me, dragging me down into the dark.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:49.159
- My brother. - It's just the dream again. That's all.

00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:56.875
It's just the dream again.

00:07:05.884 --> 00:07:07.052
She saw it.

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:12.097
She said I would die, that I ruined everything.

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:13.308
No.

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:24.819
Mother.

00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:57.768
None may enter, save at our queen's direction.

00:07:57.769 --> 00:08:00.939
It is a matter of some delicacy.

00:08:02.565 --> 00:08:06.111
I'm not certain how familiar you are with disorders of the...

00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:09.613
Female persuasion.

00:08:09.614 --> 00:08:10.699
Hm?

00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:28.132
I must thank you again for your loyalty, Grand Maester.

00:08:28.133 --> 00:08:30.259
I flatter myself to think that I have ever been

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.137
A faithful servant to Your Grace.

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.390
More than that, you've been a friend.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.227
But we have now a new queen.

00:08:41.146 --> 00:08:44.940
And I find myself under some scrutiny.

00:08:44.941 --> 00:08:50.154
I fear I can no longer offer you assistance after today

00:08:50.155 --> 00:08:52.365
Without making the proper disclosures.

00:08:54.325 --> 00:08:55.493
I understand.

00:09:10.175 --> 00:09:11.676
I don't want it.

00:09:12.802 --> 00:09:13.887
You must.

00:09:14.929 --> 00:09:17.306
It could be a boy. Do you see?

00:09:17.307 --> 00:09:19.184
Aegon's heir, a rival to Joffrey.

00:09:20.143 --> 00:09:21.686
To Rhaenyra herself.

00:09:26.858 --> 00:09:29.069
She will kill it. She will have no choice.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.196
Or if she does not, she will take it from you.

00:09:32.197 --> 00:09:34.615
Aemond still lives, as far as we know.

00:09:34.616 --> 00:09:35.908
He's at Harrenhal.

00:09:35.909 --> 00:09:37.659
No, he was there, but he has fled.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.829
- He's vanished. - I have seen him.

00:09:41.122 --> 00:09:44.250
He burns, but without fire.

00:09:50.381 --> 00:09:55.095
If Aemond threatens Rhaenyra's rule, she will use the child as her shield.

00:09:56.513 --> 00:09:58.889
I can't do it.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.725
Helaena, please. Please.

00:10:01.851 --> 00:10:03.812
For your own sake, do you not wish to be free?

00:10:04.813 --> 00:10:06.064
I can't.

00:10:07.565 --> 00:10:10.109
- No. No. - Think of it, think of it as a cup of tea.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.735
Nothing more.

00:10:11.736 --> 00:10:13.403
But it isn't.

00:10:13.404 --> 00:10:17.032
No. No, it's not. Listen to me. Listen to me, it is a blessing.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:19.953
It is a remedy taught to the masters of the Citadel.

00:10:20.954 --> 00:10:23.580
It has delivered me from disgrace and ruin.

00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:26.083
It has delivered Rhaenyra herself when she was young.

00:10:26.084 --> 00:10:27.669
And it will deliver you, too.

00:10:29.587 --> 00:10:31.004
- Helaena. Please, please. - No.

00:10:31.005 --> 00:10:33.048
Listen to me.

00:10:33.049 --> 00:10:34.800
Will you bear a child

00:10:34.801 --> 00:10:38.095
Who will be never more than a hostage or a pawn?

00:10:38.096 --> 00:10:39.264
It's mine!

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:42.350
It's my own, it's mine!

00:10:48.731 --> 00:10:50.858
I had hoped a seat on the council would suffice

00:10:50.859 --> 00:10:52.943
As recompense for House Frey's loyalty.

00:10:52.944 --> 00:10:57.281
But Harrenhal was to be our recompense, payment for giving your Winter Wolves

00:10:57.282 --> 00:11:00.075
Passage across the Twins, promised by your own son.

00:11:00.076 --> 00:11:02.494
- My son is dead. - And now, I discover

00:11:02.495 --> 00:11:05.205
That you have pledged our castle as a trophy,

00:11:05.206 --> 00:11:07.416
Free to any hedge knight who can bring you the head

00:11:07.417 --> 00:11:10.002
- of Aemond Targaryen. - You, yourself, are welcome to try.

00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:12.671
Cregan Stark's army has crossed the Trident,

00:11:12.672 --> 00:11:15.924
And we expect the crown's word to be honored,

00:11:15.925 --> 00:11:18.635
No matter if some grubby sellsword

00:11:18.636 --> 00:11:21.389
Has dubbed himself Lord of Harrenhal in the meanwhile.

00:11:26.644 --> 00:11:28.395
For now, however,

00:11:28.396 --> 00:11:31.065
I would be pleased to join Your Grace's council.

00:11:37.238 --> 00:11:39.781
<i>What could anyone possibly want in Wendish Town?</i>

00:11:39.782 --> 00:11:44.286
Not Wendish Town itself, Your Grace, but a small village at the outskirts.

00:11:44.287 --> 00:11:45.996
There were several farms burned,

00:11:45.997 --> 00:11:48.582
And the men we talked to were certain it was Vhagar herself.

00:11:48.583 --> 00:11:51.043
The Sea Snake's bastard, now a dragonrider.

00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:52.920
- That's his brother. - Lord Darry is our ally.

00:11:52.921 --> 00:11:55.255
Aemond may be provoking us.

00:11:55.256 --> 00:11:57.591
By sacking a farm or three? To what end?

00:11:57.592 --> 00:11:59.092
Dragons need to eat.

00:11:59.093 --> 00:12:00.677
The White Worm, she was called.

00:12:00.678 --> 00:12:03.096
But they are fugitives. We will root them out soon enough.

00:12:03.097 --> 00:12:05.099
- The whore. - Mm-hmm.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.648
There was a skirmish last night at the Dragon Gate.

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:14.274
Horses were required to dispel it.

00:12:14.275 --> 00:12:15.817
If only the Lady Mysaria had been there

00:12:15.818 --> 00:12:17.861
With her promised bread and ladlefuls of stew.

00:12:17.862 --> 00:12:20.656
Or if, by some miracle, the king consort's City Watch

00:12:20.657 --> 00:12:24.785
Had shown a penny's worth of restraint pursuing the pettiest of crimes,

00:12:24.786 --> 00:12:27.454
- the pettiest of criminals-- - Did anyone see where Vhagar flew?

00:12:27.455 --> 00:12:29.289
We went with all speed to take up the trail,

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:30.749
But it was two days cold.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.626
Once again, Aemond is nowhere to be found.

00:12:32.627 --> 00:12:36.380
Two of our gold cloaks were found dead in the street this morning.

00:12:36.381 --> 00:12:38.507
Put to the blade by an unknown hand.

00:12:38.508 --> 00:12:39.675
Where was this?

00:12:39.676 --> 00:12:42.010
- Flea Bottom. - Flea Bottom.

00:12:42.011 --> 00:12:44.054
Mm, has ever been a realm unto itself.

00:12:44.055 --> 00:12:47.933
Quite ungovernable, full of undesirables.

00:12:47.934 --> 00:12:51.228
Vhagar appears while Ormund Hightower

00:12:51.229 --> 00:12:53.313
Gathers himself at Tumbleton to some hidden purpose.

00:12:53.314 --> 00:12:55.440
We need not waste our sweat fretting over a fox

00:12:55.441 --> 00:12:57.192
Gone to ground. If you will not burn him...

00:12:57.193 --> 00:12:58.694
- He is not a f-- - ...then my army

00:12:58.695 --> 00:13:00.112
Will root him out soon enough.

00:13:00.113 --> 00:13:02.030
As to that, there is fresh news

00:13:02.031 --> 00:13:04.283
From Lord Tully's camp.

00:13:04.284 --> 00:13:06.243
Their march has been slowed by interference

00:13:06.244 --> 00:13:08.453
From Ser Criston Cole and his men.

00:13:08.454 --> 00:13:11.707
River crossings are being burned before the army can reach them.

00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:13.333
Go back to the Riverlands.

00:13:13.334 --> 00:13:15.460
If Aemond has shown himself once, he may do so again.

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:18.255
Take no risk, but ascertain his path, his purpose.

00:13:18.256 --> 00:13:19.715
If I may, Your Grace.

00:13:19.716 --> 00:13:22.843
We arrived back only this morning.

00:13:22.844 --> 00:13:25.095
The Lady Baela has not eaten, much less slept.

00:13:25.096 --> 00:13:26.930
I am more than ready to fly.

00:13:26.931 --> 00:13:28.557
It will not serve us if your eyes are weary

00:13:28.558 --> 00:13:30.475
And your beast fatigued.

00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:31.936
I will send Daemon.

00:13:33.187 --> 00:13:36.565
I will go once I have dealt with this business in the city.

00:13:36.566 --> 00:13:38.817
Our fallen soldiers. An accounting must be made.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:41.278
- Do you not agree? - I am able, Your Grace.

00:13:41.279 --> 00:13:42.988
The loss to our City Watch

00:13:42.989 --> 00:13:45.783
Is a crime, to be sure, but Ser Luthor will investigate.

00:13:46.659 --> 00:13:49.286
- It is not a matter for the crown. - They are my men.

00:13:49.287 --> 00:13:51.998
And we depend on those men now to secure your rule.

00:13:54.292 --> 00:13:56.544
Especially since their wages have been withheld.

00:14:00.048 --> 00:14:01.549
- Your Grace. - Not now.

00:14:02.925 --> 00:14:04.344
Is it always like this?

00:14:05.136 --> 00:14:06.720
Mm.

00:14:06.721 --> 00:14:07.972
Daemon.

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:12.517
Have I somehow found myself back on Dragonstone?

00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:14.978
That my voice must again compete with yours?

00:14:14.979 --> 00:14:17.189
On the contrary. I have pledged to fulfill your command.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:18.106
Just...

00:14:18.107 --> 00:14:19.024
Later.

00:14:19.025 --> 00:14:21.360
I'm in no mood to jest. What does it make of me

00:14:21.361 --> 00:14:23.695
If you will obey me only at a time and place of your own choosing?

00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:25.447
You are the queen.

00:14:25.448 --> 00:14:27.324
I act in your interest.

00:14:27.325 --> 00:14:30.118
Good. My interest is Vhagar.

00:14:30.119 --> 00:14:31.703
Mine too. But we have time enough.

00:14:31.704 --> 00:14:34.873
Aemond is afraid. He has fled once already before you.

00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:37.793
- We are in no danger. - There is treachery somewhere,

00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:39.503
And I seek to uncover it.

00:14:39.504 --> 00:14:41.838
What you seek is revenge.

00:14:41.839 --> 00:14:45.300
And gods know I do not grudge you that, but revenge may wait.

00:14:45.301 --> 00:14:47.594
At this moment, there is a disturbance in your city,

00:14:47.595 --> 00:14:49.806
And you, yourself, are its likely cause.

00:14:52.266 --> 00:14:54.726
I did not ask Ser Luthor to be brutal.

00:14:54.727 --> 00:14:57.437
You need not have asked him anything at all.

00:14:57.438 --> 00:14:59.898
Will you let yourself be rattled by vapid taunts,

00:14:59.899 --> 00:15:01.733
By the painting of stripes on tavern walls?

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:04.778
They are more than taunts. They are an insult to my sons.

00:15:04.779 --> 00:15:06.780
A challenge to my very legitimacy.

00:15:06.781 --> 00:15:08.698
You are the Queen of Dragons.

00:15:08.699 --> 00:15:10.826
Your strength is your legitimacy.

00:15:10.827 --> 00:15:12.078
Your Grace?

00:15:18.668 --> 00:15:20.044
Glad news.

00:15:20.711 --> 00:15:23.548
Young Prince Joffrey has returned this hour from the Vale.

00:15:26.467 --> 00:15:28.719
I'm told he's asked for you.

00:15:30.388 --> 00:15:34.809
I will come to him when I'm able. I'm sure he's tired.

00:15:40.481 --> 00:15:42.190
It is long past the nightingale.

00:15:42.191 --> 00:15:44.109
I don't care.

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.570
Which way is West?

00:15:46.529 --> 00:15:47.655
I have no idea.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.704
- If I may say, Your Grace-- - I'm not going back.

00:15:55.705 --> 00:15:58.415
- We have nowhere else to go. - You heard what I did.

00:15:58.416 --> 00:16:00.542
Vhagar has been sighted at Wendish Town.

00:16:00.543 --> 00:16:02.586
Two days ago. Who knows where she may be now?

00:16:02.587 --> 00:16:05.213
Well, Harrenhal, then. Someone there will know something.

00:16:05.214 --> 00:16:07.549
Look, Aemond must have left a message or a sign.

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:09.718
- We can pick up his trail. - It's 100 leagues

00:16:09.719 --> 00:16:11.261
To Harrenhal, Your Grace, and the fields

00:16:11.262 --> 00:16:13.597
And woods are teeming with Rivermen.

00:16:13.598 --> 00:16:16.475
This is more than a folly. It is dangerous.

00:16:16.476 --> 00:16:19.479
Fucking seven fucking hells!

00:16:21.147 --> 00:16:23.773
What would you do if you found him, hm?

00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:27.611
Your brother is a coiled viper, and you are...

00:16:27.612 --> 00:16:31.656
You are hungry, and broken, and spent, and we are alone.

00:16:31.657 --> 00:16:33.074
If we were to be discovered--

00:16:33.075 --> 00:16:35.244
Stop telling me what I can't do!

00:16:38.581 --> 00:16:39.999
This is his fault.

00:16:41.209 --> 00:16:42.210
Everything.

00:16:43.294 --> 00:16:48.256
Every one of my miseries is of his making, and I swear before the Warrior himself,

00:16:48.257 --> 00:16:52.720
I'm going to find him and fucking kill him or die in the attempt.

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:54.931
Hm.

00:17:18.496 --> 00:17:19.997
You know me, I think.

00:17:22.291 --> 00:17:23.500
By reputation.

00:17:23.501 --> 00:17:28.672
It is my privilege now to listen to the whispers of the Red Keep.

00:17:28.673 --> 00:17:31.049
- The guests you receive... - What is it that you want?

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:33.844
...and the gifts they bring.

00:17:35.763 --> 00:17:37.223
Show it to me.

00:17:53.322 --> 00:17:55.115
My daughter has been unwell.

00:17:55.116 --> 00:17:57.534
As you see, she suffers terrible headaches.

00:17:57.535 --> 00:18:01.079
The maester is kind enough to tend to her.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.332
And yet the flask is full.

00:18:08.629 --> 00:18:10.840
I took a lover after Viserys.

00:18:11.841 --> 00:18:15.428
The queen herself knows the truth of it. I was careless, to my shame.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:21.934
It's a difficult thing, but I should no longer delay.

00:18:33.988 --> 00:18:37.157
Was he a lord or a commoner?

00:18:37.158 --> 00:18:38.993
Or perhaps both?

00:18:41.912 --> 00:18:44.498
I must appeal to you, Lady Mysaria.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.419
You of all people must understand the...

00:18:49.545 --> 00:18:52.423
The indignities we women endure.

00:18:54.467 --> 00:18:56.676
There is surely no need for this to be spoken of again.

00:18:56.677 --> 00:18:59.639
You would not, of course, seek to deceive the queen.

00:19:02.266 --> 00:19:04.143
I am her prisoner.

00:19:06.270 --> 00:19:08.189
As you were once, if I'm not mistaken.

00:19:14.987 --> 00:19:16.739
As you say.

00:19:23.537 --> 00:19:24.996
Have you ever seen the Hightower

00:19:24.997 --> 00:19:26.457
At Oldtown, Ser Criston?

00:19:27.416 --> 00:19:28.626
I've heard tell of it.

00:19:29.794 --> 00:19:31.796
Ormund and I had a game,

00:19:32.588 --> 00:19:33.923
To "run the tower."

00:19:35.216 --> 00:19:37.175
You'd start at the base before dawn

00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:39.511
And aim to be the first one to see the sun rise

00:19:39.512 --> 00:19:41.096
From the beacon.

00:19:41.097 --> 00:19:42.932
Of course, I let him win.

00:19:43.974 --> 00:19:45.768
He was a thin-skinned twat even then.

00:19:46.769 --> 00:19:48.687
Mm.

00:19:48.688 --> 00:19:54.067
At that moment, when the sun rises over the Seven Kingdoms,

00:19:54.068 --> 00:19:55.986
Hundreds and hundreds of miles...

00:19:57.697 --> 00:19:59.990
I hope to show it to you one day.

00:20:01.701 --> 00:20:03.952
You could make a home at Oldtown, Ser Criston.

00:20:03.953 --> 00:20:06.747
A knight of your stature would be most welcome...

00:20:08.541 --> 00:20:10.167
To serve our house there.

00:20:16.674 --> 00:20:18.592
Halt! Stay back!

00:20:23.889 --> 00:20:25.599
Stay clear!

00:20:28.436 --> 00:20:29.770
Hold your ground!

00:20:31.147 --> 00:20:32.523
Stand your ground!

00:20:42.408 --> 00:20:44.577
Crow's feet.

00:20:45.786 --> 00:20:47.036
Gods.

00:20:47.037 --> 00:20:48.789
Are they ahead of us?

00:21:40.549 --> 00:21:43.259
<i>Your hand was heavier than warranted by the crime.</i>

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:46.429
I was well schooled in those manners, was I not?

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:48.098
I had the finest of captains.

00:21:49.642 --> 00:21:52.477
In any case, the queen wanted it stopped.

00:21:52.478 --> 00:21:55.104
The queen's son is dead. She must be excused her impulses.

00:21:55.105 --> 00:21:58.233
- Oh, you'd have me refuse her? - No, rather temper her.

00:21:58.234 --> 00:21:59.234
Tend to her humors.

00:21:59.235 --> 00:22:01.861
Not every whim needs to be pursued with equal vigor.

00:22:01.862 --> 00:22:04.697
You know, they cut their bowels as well as their throat.

00:22:04.698 --> 00:22:06.282
Did they tell you that?

00:22:06.283 --> 00:22:09.411
Good men dying in agony in their own shit.

00:22:10.412 --> 00:22:12.038
We will pay the villains back in kind.

00:22:12.039 --> 00:22:13.957
What is the mood among the men?

00:22:13.958 --> 00:22:15.917
They complain about their wages, or lack of them.

00:22:15.918 --> 00:22:17.418
I shall address them.

00:22:17.419 --> 00:22:19.921
A rousing speech from the Rogue Prince himself.

00:22:19.922 --> 00:22:22.215
I'm not sure that's gonna make up for a steady wage anymore.

00:22:22.216 --> 00:22:24.133
If I lead them, they will follow.

00:22:24.134 --> 00:22:26.177
It's been a minute

00:22:26.178 --> 00:22:28.471
Since you were the Prince of Flea Bottom.

00:22:28.472 --> 00:22:31.767
Most of the men were in swaddling clothes when you--

00:23:32.703 --> 00:23:34.120
What is our standing?

00:23:34.121 --> 00:23:36.456
Battlements are being raised with haste, my lord.

00:23:36.457 --> 00:23:40.919
But we lack in timber, and men, and time.

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:43.046
Then levy more conscripts,

00:23:43.047 --> 00:23:45.673
And fell every tree from here to Bitterbridge.

00:23:45.674 --> 00:23:47.300
We must secure our walls.

00:23:47.301 --> 00:23:48.928
Rhaenyra's host is surely on the march.

00:23:50.304 --> 00:23:53.432
The maester tells me you've been most assiduous in your lessons.

00:23:55.309 --> 00:23:57.518
We are making a study on my forebears

00:23:57.519 --> 00:23:59.312
On the Hightower side.

00:23:59.313 --> 00:24:02.899
I mean, their battles, their enemies.

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:04.943
It has been three days now spent in the pursuit

00:24:04.944 --> 00:24:06.320
Of these dry histories.

00:24:09.782 --> 00:24:11.325
Dry, did you say?

00:24:13.786 --> 00:24:15.537
No. Of course not.

00:24:18.415 --> 00:24:21.250
Or rather, they may seem dry at first glance,

00:24:21.251 --> 00:24:22.795
But to learn fr...

00:24:24.088 --> 00:24:28.841
To venerate our ancestors, that is a noble task.

00:24:28.842 --> 00:24:30.469
And I'm grateful for it.

00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:33.346
Good.

00:24:33.347 --> 00:24:35.516
It would please me to hear you recite.

00:24:39.687 --> 00:24:42.188
We have parsed out the conflicts

00:24:42.189 --> 00:24:46.859
Between House Greyjoy and Houses Peake

00:24:46.860 --> 00:24:48.945
And Osgrey and Gardener,

00:24:48.946 --> 00:24:50.154
House Dayne of Dorne--

00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:51.699
And Meria Martell?

00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:55.494
The Yellow Toad of Dorne.

00:24:58.831 --> 00:25:00.666
I should have a word with your tutor.

00:25:02.292 --> 00:25:04.627
She was the only woman ever to have been gifted

00:25:04.628 --> 00:25:07.006
With a truly military mind.

00:25:09.174 --> 00:25:12.261
Though the gods divested her of beauty in turn.

00:25:13.095 --> 00:25:14.679
A blind princess.

00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:17.766
Hideous, hairless, thick of waist.

00:25:19.393 --> 00:25:21.729
She does not sound so formidable.

00:25:24.314 --> 00:25:26.357
When Aegon the Conqueror claimed her lands,

00:25:26.358 --> 00:25:27.693
She refused to submit.

00:25:29.028 --> 00:25:30.987
She declared him a usurper.

00:25:30.988 --> 00:25:32.530
And all those that marched for him,

00:25:32.531 --> 00:25:33.991
Traitors to the Seven Kingdoms.

00:25:35.367 --> 00:25:40.372
And she swore that Dorne would ever be unbowed, unbent.

00:25:47.046 --> 00:25:50.214
A great host descended from the Red Mountains,

00:25:50.215 --> 00:25:52.592
We Hightowers regrettably among them.

00:25:52.593 --> 00:25:54.510
Meria poisoned her own wells,

00:25:54.511 --> 00:25:57.264
Hid her soldiers in the very sand of the desert.

00:25:58.390 --> 00:26:00.475
Her castle, when they found it, was empty.

00:26:00.476 --> 00:26:03.019
They thought that she was vanquished.

00:26:03.020 --> 00:26:07.066
But she rose up out of the darkness and slaughtered them in their beds.

00:26:09.276 --> 00:26:12.404
Is she a hero, then? Or a villain?

00:26:19.286 --> 00:26:22.872
The Targaryens knew nothing of our civilization,

00:26:22.873 --> 00:26:24.457
The Faith, the Citadel.

00:26:24.458 --> 00:26:26.292
What they had,

00:26:26.293 --> 00:26:29.755
What they still have, is strength.

00:26:31.090 --> 00:26:33.425
Their armies, the obscenity of their dragons.

00:26:34.259 --> 00:26:36.845
Meria Martell outwitted her enemy.

00:26:37.805 --> 00:26:41.975
A cunning mind can resist the most savage of beasts.

00:26:43.393 --> 00:26:46.939
And Dorne remains unbroken even today.

00:27:04.832 --> 00:27:05.999
I was lucky.

00:27:08.210 --> 00:27:09.461
Let us start again.

00:27:32.317 --> 00:27:34.736
Never apologize for victory.

00:27:43.912 --> 00:27:45.497
I have had these made.

00:27:56.091 --> 00:27:57.467
Do you think it a good likeness?

00:28:00.137 --> 00:28:04.056
You are the sign our allies have been waiting for.

00:28:04.057 --> 00:28:07.936
The son of Viserys, the beacon shining from the High Tower.

00:28:09.313 --> 00:28:13.066
From the lowliest of the faithful to Borros Baratheon himself.

00:28:19.907 --> 00:28:22.326
Oh. No, you can't touch that.

00:28:23.577 --> 00:28:24.786
Helaena?

00:28:27.122 --> 00:28:28.290
Do you know why?

00:28:29.291 --> 00:28:33.211
They eat the leaves of the nightshade, but that would be death for you or me.

00:28:33.212 --> 00:28:34.503
It's a puzzle.

00:28:34.504 --> 00:28:35.923
Jaehaera, come with me.

00:28:41.637 --> 00:28:42.930
Come.

00:28:47.643 --> 00:28:49.894
Listen now, dearest. We must leave here.

00:28:49.895 --> 00:28:51.355
This very evening.

00:28:52.981 --> 00:28:54.774
There seems to be some trouble in the city,

00:28:54.775 --> 00:28:58.152
And some of Rhaenyra's soldiers must go to help the City Watch.

00:28:58.153 --> 00:28:59.947
We will have one guard tonight instead of two.

00:29:03.951 --> 00:29:05.326
Your necklace.

00:29:05.327 --> 00:29:07.371
I tendered it to a maid. She will help us.

00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:11.333
There is a hidden door that leads out in Aemond's chamber.

00:29:12.251 --> 00:29:13.794
Below the keep and beyond its walls.

00:29:14.711 --> 00:29:17.047
The one the men used when they came to kill my boy?

00:29:19.174 --> 00:29:20.592
The room is Baela's now.

00:29:21.843 --> 00:29:23.595
And she will no doubt be out hunting.

00:29:25.555 --> 00:29:26.847
With luck, we may escape

00:29:26.848 --> 00:29:29.141
And melt into the streets of King's Landing.

00:29:29.142 --> 00:29:30.727
And Jaehaera?

00:29:32.354 --> 00:29:33.939
Her room is guarded.

00:29:34.815 --> 00:29:37.693
If she were to cry out, even once...

00:29:38.944 --> 00:29:40.946
- then that would be the end. - I will not leave her.

00:29:42.656 --> 00:29:45.783
The road ahead will not be safe for her.

00:29:45.784 --> 00:29:50.663
Here, she has nursemaids to care for her, and Rhaenyra will not harm her.

00:29:50.664 --> 00:29:52.666
Her rivals would never raise a girl up to rule, and...

00:29:53.959 --> 00:29:55.668
And it might be prudent,

00:29:55.669 --> 00:29:58.296
In fact, for the queen to take the child to ward.

00:29:58.297 --> 00:30:01.675
We may even be able to-- to send for her one day.

00:30:08.890 --> 00:30:10.642
You look away when you lie.

00:30:15.439 --> 00:30:19.234
It has been days since Vhagar was here. She feeds, then eludes us.

00:30:20.402 --> 00:30:23.405
We have traversed the Trident 50 times in the last fortnight.

00:30:24.656 --> 00:30:26.741
For now, we must rest.

00:30:26.742 --> 00:30:29.785
Could Aemond be crossing into the Westerlands to hide?

00:30:29.786 --> 00:30:31.620
The Lannisters are allies,

00:30:31.621 --> 00:30:33.748
And there are caves and crannies aplenty in those mountains.

00:30:33.749 --> 00:30:35.666
And I'll be pleased to explore them with you

00:30:35.667 --> 00:30:37.793
When you've had a sleep and a meal.

00:30:37.794 --> 00:30:39.296
- He may be moving by night-- - Baela!

00:30:42.716 --> 00:30:44.842
- My lady. - It is well enough for you.

00:30:44.843 --> 00:30:48.387
The queen sees you as her talisman, a sign from the gods, but I--

00:30:48.388 --> 00:30:49.764
It wasn't your fault.

00:30:49.765 --> 00:30:51.558
She won't look at me.

00:30:53.268 --> 00:30:54.895
And I cannot say I blame her.

00:30:57.064 --> 00:30:59.273
The truth is, Addam, I wanted to go.

00:30:59.274 --> 00:31:01.026
I saw myself a hero.

00:31:02.402 --> 00:31:04.988
Turning the tide of a great battle and...

00:31:06.323 --> 00:31:08.032
Proving my worth to the realm.

00:31:08.033 --> 00:31:10.910
I have the same desire, as do others.

00:31:10.911 --> 00:31:13.246
It is pride, and I am punished for it.

00:31:15.040 --> 00:31:16.541
My future was ordained.

00:31:17.834 --> 00:31:19.252
I was one day to be queen.

00:31:20.170 --> 00:31:22.630
My path lay straight before me, and now--

00:31:22.631 --> 00:31:24.382
Your path has vanished.

00:31:24.383 --> 00:31:26.134
Though it has been replaced, perhaps.

00:31:27.761 --> 00:31:29.178
By an adventure.

00:31:29.179 --> 00:31:31.889
I'll be married off, likely enough,

00:31:31.890 --> 00:31:35.684
To some ancient, self-regarding lord in Pyke,

00:31:35.685 --> 00:31:37.520
With enough hoarded gold to pay Rhaenyra's debts.

00:31:37.521 --> 00:31:39.356
And then, I'll come and find you.

00:31:40.357 --> 00:31:41.733
And we'll fly to exile.

00:31:43.860 --> 00:31:45.445
But only if we eat first.

00:31:51.993 --> 00:31:53.412
Vhagar!

00:31:55.163 --> 00:31:56.415
She's gone.

00:31:58.458 --> 00:31:59.875
No.

00:31:59.876 --> 00:32:02.670
No, no, she will not abandon me.

00:32:02.671 --> 00:32:06.633
I know only that she flew in the night and I did not see where.

00:32:07.717 --> 00:32:09.302
Maybe she was afraid.

00:32:15.350 --> 00:32:16.935
Am I a prisoner?

00:32:49.217 --> 00:32:50.594
No.

00:32:55.557 --> 00:32:57.476
Without her, I'm nothing.

00:32:58.643 --> 00:33:01.271
- You are mistaken. - I must find her.

00:33:02.814 --> 00:33:06.234
And how will you do that if the dragon has fled?

00:33:08.111 --> 00:33:09.821
The queen hunts her as well.

00:33:12.908 --> 00:33:14.575
The queen?

00:33:14.576 --> 00:33:16.870
I told you, King's Landing has fallen.

00:33:18.371 --> 00:33:20.499
I thought I dreamed it.

00:33:25.378 --> 00:33:26.505
Aegon?

00:33:27.380 --> 00:33:29.341
The queen says he's dead.

00:33:30.467 --> 00:33:31.718
And that you killed him.

00:33:36.181 --> 00:33:38.600
Though I do not know how much of that to believe.

00:33:40.894 --> 00:33:44.397
He is dead because he will not let me be.

00:33:49.694 --> 00:33:50.946
He...

00:33:51.780 --> 00:33:53.240
He tormented me.

00:33:56.409 --> 00:33:57.911
My childhood...

00:33:58.828 --> 00:34:00.205
I worshiped him.

00:34:09.130 --> 00:34:10.757
And yet our mother...

00:34:13.843 --> 00:34:15.136
Sometimes...

00:34:16.471 --> 00:34:18.348
The child that grieves her...

00:34:19.808 --> 00:34:21.851
Is the one a mother loves best.

00:34:23.103 --> 00:34:24.104
Hm?

00:34:27.983 --> 00:34:29.317
Who are you?

00:34:32.028 --> 00:34:33.863
One that has been grieved.

00:34:42.247 --> 00:34:43.373
Go on.

00:34:44.291 --> 00:34:45.292
Say it.

00:34:48.420 --> 00:34:49.838
My dragon is dead.

00:34:50.797 --> 00:34:52.215
I'm a pathetic cripple.

00:34:53.216 --> 00:34:57.761
And there is no possible scenario in which I make it to Wendish Town

00:34:57.762 --> 00:34:59.763
To kill my stupid fucking brother.

00:34:59.764 --> 00:35:03.226
Now as you should say, should we-- should we return to the camp, Your Grace?

00:35:04.853 --> 00:35:07.771
I do not care to be discovered here unguarded,

00:35:07.772 --> 00:35:09.189
And less so when darkness falls.

00:35:09.190 --> 00:35:13.236
He was Cole's little pet, do you remember? A prodigy with the sword.

00:35:14.112 --> 00:35:16.448
Father withdrew me from the tournaments, of course.

00:35:17.240 --> 00:35:20.701
Can't even remember the pretext anymore.

00:35:20.702 --> 00:35:23.370
Probably just afraid that I'd fall off my horse.

00:35:23.371 --> 00:35:26.415
So, I had to sit and applaud him.

00:35:26.416 --> 00:35:28.251
Aemond the champion.

00:35:30.211 --> 00:35:32.212
And such a quick student.

00:35:32.213 --> 00:35:34.591
Fucking fluent in High Valyrian.

00:35:42.390 --> 00:35:46.311
I'm sure he thought I was a terrible king, but what I could have been if I was...

00:35:47.062 --> 00:35:49.563
...given his fucking advantages.

00:35:49.564 --> 00:35:52.441
And Mother indulged him. She loved him more, is the truth of it.

00:35:52.442 --> 00:35:55.819
Poor darling Aemond and his scabby little eye.

00:35:55.820 --> 00:35:58.657
And now he's killed me, and the whole fucking realm knows it.

00:36:05.455 --> 00:36:07.998
- I must say, Your Grace. - What?

00:36:07.999 --> 00:36:10.418
All this time we've been together...

00:36:12.754 --> 00:36:14.922
From the moment you were injured, in fact,

00:36:14.923 --> 00:36:17.759
Flying drunk into a battle to which you were not invited...

00:36:18.677 --> 00:36:22.305
You've done nothing but whinge

00:36:23.431 --> 00:36:28.394
And self-flagellate with a tenacity I find astonishing.

00:36:28.395 --> 00:36:32.106
You, who had every advantage in life.

00:36:32.107 --> 00:36:36.151
You, who had every chance to shine.

00:36:36.152 --> 00:36:41.615
Firstborn son, prince of the realm, the finest tutors, the finest knights

00:36:41.616 --> 00:36:43.243
Instructing you in the sword.

00:36:44.202 --> 00:36:47.205
A dragon so beautiful, they named him after the sun itself.

00:36:49.916 --> 00:36:52.752
You could have risen to greatness.

00:36:53.670 --> 00:36:58.174
But instead, you trampled your birthright in the mud.

00:37:00.927 --> 00:37:02.220
You lazed...

00:37:03.430 --> 00:37:05.765
Reveling in mediocrity...

00:37:06.933 --> 00:37:09.226
Fucking anything in sight and drinking yourself

00:37:09.227 --> 00:37:11.896
Into oblivion with your sycophantic friends.

00:37:16.317 --> 00:37:17.819
I will tell you the truth.

00:37:19.279 --> 00:37:20.864
You were a terrible king.

00:37:22.615 --> 00:37:23.950
But worse than that...

00:37:25.034 --> 00:37:28.705
You are a terrible man.

00:37:44.512 --> 00:37:45.638
Don't.

00:37:47.640 --> 00:37:49.184
They said you were here.

00:37:49.851 --> 00:37:51.351
I thought there was some mistake.

00:37:51.352 --> 00:37:57.149
They require of me, perhaps, just some show of deference, or regard.

00:37:57.150 --> 00:37:59.110
- The people or the Seven? - Both.

00:38:00.487 --> 00:38:02.989
There can be no harm in it, at the least. You could try it.

00:38:17.420 --> 00:38:19.838
Four of my men lie dead.

00:38:19.839 --> 00:38:21.465
Six, if you count the two from yesterday.

00:38:21.466 --> 00:38:23.802
All gold cloaks, all killed in the same way.

00:38:24.677 --> 00:38:25.845
Throats cut.

00:40:44.776 --> 00:40:46.194
You are tired.

00:40:50.073 --> 00:40:51.865
You hear the wind in these vaulted towers

00:40:51.866 --> 00:40:53.993
And imagine their omens when there are none.

00:40:56.829 --> 00:40:58.623
Hm? These are men only.

00:40:59.666 --> 00:41:01.751
- Nothing more. - Then why can't you find them?

00:41:30.363 --> 00:41:32.240
You are more than this.

00:41:36.577 --> 00:41:38.537
<i>This costs us precious time.</i>

00:41:38.538 --> 00:41:39.913
That is no doubt their goal.

00:41:39.914 --> 00:41:43.667
They knew we would leave the road when we abandoned our mounts.

00:41:43.668 --> 00:41:46.837
This land may be theirs, but even they could not cause thorns

00:41:46.838 --> 00:41:50.424
And brambles to spring from the earth in our path.

00:41:50.425 --> 00:41:52.009
And men are talking of desertion.

00:41:52.010 --> 00:41:54.721
Ser Criston. Friend.

00:41:56.472 --> 00:41:59.391
They see no sense in continuing with this plan and to speak truth,

00:41:59.392 --> 00:42:01.309
Nor do I. We grow weak.

00:42:01.310 --> 00:42:03.604
- Stoney Sept still lies far ahead. - Mm.

00:42:09.318 --> 00:42:10.945
If we leave the track here...

00:42:11.863 --> 00:42:13.613
Cut straight through the lowlands toward the crossing,

00:42:13.614 --> 00:42:15.533
We may yet still gain a day or two over Tully's host.

00:42:52.528 --> 00:42:54.363
Just hire the fucking ship.

00:43:02.163 --> 00:43:03.790
What ship might that be?

00:43:05.792 --> 00:43:07.293
Seven hells.

00:43:16.219 --> 00:43:17.804
He's gone. My lady, be quick.

00:43:30.775 --> 00:43:33.860
You said the nurse would meet us with Jaehaera.

00:43:33.861 --> 00:43:35.237
And so she will, at the other end.

00:43:35.238 --> 00:43:37.073
- Where? - Come, now. Quickly.

00:43:46.916 --> 00:43:49.293
Did you imagine I wouldn't be watching?

00:43:52.088 --> 00:43:54.881
So it is she who is with child.

00:43:54.882 --> 00:43:56.716
An inconvenient heir.

00:43:56.717 --> 00:43:59.177
There is no need for Rhaenyra to hear of what transpired tonight.

00:43:59.178 --> 00:44:02.139
I will keep no more secrets from the queen.

00:44:02.140 --> 00:44:04.267
And what will be the result if you tell her?

00:44:05.601 --> 00:44:07.395
We are already at her mercy.

00:44:08.563 --> 00:44:10.939
In but a short time, Helaena's condition will make itself known,

00:44:10.940 --> 00:44:13.066
As these things cannot help but do.

00:44:13.067 --> 00:44:14.819
It is not for me to decide.

00:44:17.196 --> 00:44:19.157
I heard tell of the White Worm.

00:44:21.075 --> 00:44:21.951
Years ago.

00:44:22.743 --> 00:44:26.205
She dealt in secrets and extortion, and I knew men who feared her.

00:44:28.249 --> 00:44:31.751
She had the cunning to play all sides, not just lapdog to the queen.

00:44:31.752 --> 00:44:35.005
These are rich words in the mouth of a Hightower.

00:44:35.006 --> 00:44:38.551
I simply urge you to think of yourself.

00:44:39.886 --> 00:44:42.096
There is good in Rhaenyra, but...

00:44:43.139 --> 00:44:45.016
The crown is a weight that crushes.

00:44:49.854 --> 00:44:51.730
Rhaenyra will do in the end what she has to do,

00:44:51.731 --> 00:44:53.816
And what she has to do will be dire.

00:44:55.443 --> 00:44:57.527
There is only one who can walk that path with her,

00:44:57.528 --> 00:44:58.904
And she chose him long ago.

00:44:58.905 --> 00:45:00.614
She knows what Daemon is.

00:45:00.615 --> 00:45:03.241
They have ever been two sides of a coin...

00:45:03.242 --> 00:45:04.744
As much as she may deny it.

00:45:07.663 --> 00:45:10.498
Her attentions may be on you now,

00:45:10.499 --> 00:45:14.253
That you bathe in the warm light of her gaze, but...

00:45:15.796 --> 00:45:19.133
Will you stake so high a wager on the whims of a dragonrider?

00:45:20.218 --> 00:45:21.552
I want to go out.

00:45:23.596 --> 00:45:25.223
- Not now, dearest. - Yes.

00:45:27.808 --> 00:45:29.392
I need to see the moon.

00:45:29.393 --> 00:45:31.145
The window will have to do.

00:45:32.605 --> 00:45:36.191
Speak, and you serve no one, you gain the queen no advantage.

00:45:36.192 --> 00:45:39.445
But if you say nothing, no harm is done.

00:45:40.488 --> 00:45:42.615
You earn yourself favor with the Hightowers...

00:45:45.618 --> 00:45:47.745
If a time should come when you have need of it.

00:46:15.189 --> 00:46:17.358
He tried to stay awake for you, Your Grace.

00:46:22.446 --> 00:46:25.115
Come on, keep moving!

00:46:25.116 --> 00:46:26.993
Keep moving now!

00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:53.269
Forward.

00:46:57.857 --> 00:47:00.818
Leave him! Leave him where he fell.

00:48:12.598 --> 00:48:14.015
Where is he?

00:48:14.016 --> 00:48:15.893
Aemond One-Eye. We know he's been here.

00:48:16.936 --> 00:48:19.063
Good ser, this has become tiresome.

00:48:20.231 --> 00:48:22.732
I'm of a mind to send a message to the queen myself.

00:48:22.733 --> 00:48:24.275
He's not here.

00:48:24.276 --> 00:48:26.486
- He has never been here. - She's lying.

00:48:26.487 --> 00:48:28.780
I've heard about you, witch.

00:48:28.781 --> 00:48:31.367
She's no witch. She's an imbecile.

00:48:32.118 --> 00:48:34.953
Cast out and wandering. Touched in the head.

00:48:34.954 --> 00:48:36.704
Though not in the cunny for too long, I think.

00:48:36.705 --> 00:48:39.916
Will you speak to me thus in the very shadow of my fortress?

00:48:39.917 --> 00:48:41.793
It's been weeks since I've had a woman.

00:48:41.794 --> 00:48:44.255
I'm going to fuck you and make you my salt wife.

00:48:58.811 --> 00:48:59.854
Ah!

00:49:24.712 --> 00:49:26.755
Seems you've taken a turn for the better.

00:49:36.891 --> 00:49:40.185
In Essos, we can secrete His Grace until the time is right for his return.

00:49:40.186 --> 00:49:43.313
But we are watched now. We can linger here no longer.

00:49:43.314 --> 00:49:45.690
- You risk his safety merely by speaking-- - An ocean passage beset

00:49:45.691 --> 00:49:49.068
By pirates, and dragons, and storms, and then what?

00:49:49.069 --> 00:49:51.404
Eating dates and incense while Westeros

00:49:51.405 --> 00:49:53.948
- is reduced to ash? - His Grace is in no state to fight.

00:49:53.949 --> 00:49:55.701
Neither would he tolerate the Braavosi heat.

00:49:56.785 --> 00:49:59.078
- The monkeys alone-- - You surprise me, Lannister.

00:49:59.079 --> 00:50:00.705
Such a distaste for the foreign.

00:50:00.706 --> 00:50:04.042
I have lived with these people. Do you forget? I've eaten with them,

00:50:04.043 --> 00:50:06.378
Fought with them, shared everything with them, even their...

00:50:08.088 --> 00:50:09.298
Yes?

00:50:10.299 --> 00:50:11.509
I know what they are.

00:50:13.511 --> 00:50:15.762
In Braavos, I have prepared the means for us

00:50:15.763 --> 00:50:18.014
To live in a manner as befits His Grace.

00:50:18.015 --> 00:50:19.807
- We can ascertain-- - He is the king, Larys.

00:50:19.808 --> 00:50:22.810
Not some chip for you to hold until such time as benefits you.

00:50:22.811 --> 00:50:25.230
- I have men riding with me-- - Sellswords.

00:50:25.231 --> 00:50:26.731
Cheaply bought, by the look of them.

00:50:26.732 --> 00:50:30.401
We need only bring him to Lannisport, where he will be sheltered.

00:50:30.402 --> 00:50:32.820
From there, we may summon and command what strength remains to us.

00:50:32.821 --> 00:50:34.531
Yes, no doubt it would be the making of the Lannisters

00:50:34.532 --> 00:50:36.824
To declare Casterly Rock the new seat of the king.

00:50:36.825 --> 00:50:38.368
Do you think even now of your own advancement?

00:50:38.369 --> 00:50:41.371
Oh, begging your pardon, most selfless of servants.

00:50:41.372 --> 00:50:43.248
I was only risking my life at sea for our common cause.

00:50:43.249 --> 00:50:44.958
Gregor, is it?

00:50:44.959 --> 00:50:47.169
It seems I missed the salient moment when His Grace made you Hand.

00:50:53.050 --> 00:50:56.136
You may call me "Your Grace."

00:51:08.649 --> 00:51:12.068
There is an evil spirit afoot. This is no man, I tell you.

00:51:12.069 --> 00:51:14.779
Do not shame yourself, Ned. We're knights, not infants.

00:51:14.780 --> 00:51:19.033
But we will find these cravens and make a grim example of them.

00:51:19.034 --> 00:51:21.953
We are hunters. Not prey.

00:51:21.954 --> 00:51:24.915
- Hunters get paid. - It's not safe out there!

00:51:27.418 --> 00:51:28.669
Enough.

00:51:30.004 --> 00:51:31.796
You and I are the protectors and keepers

00:51:31.797 --> 00:51:34.174
Of the greatest Citadel in all of Westeros.

00:51:35.676 --> 00:51:37.636
The governing seat of a mighty realm.

00:51:40.931 --> 00:51:44.101
Without the City Watch, without us...

00:51:46.478 --> 00:51:48.647
These streets would echo with the cries of insurrection.

00:51:51.025 --> 00:51:54.485
The alleys of King's Landing would boil with corruption and depravity.

00:51:54.486 --> 00:51:58.948
I look to you now to uphold your vows to the city and to the throne.

00:51:58.949 --> 00:52:03.536
Trust in your queen, and I pledge you, you will be repaid twice over

00:52:03.537 --> 00:52:05.581
For the sacrifices you make now.

00:52:08.292 --> 00:52:11.837
And in the years to come, as Dorne finally bends the knee...

00:52:14.048 --> 00:52:15.757
...as Rhaenyra's great empire grows

00:52:15.758 --> 00:52:18.176
And the Seven Kingdoms become Nine,

00:52:18.177 --> 00:52:21.472
Become Twelve, become the new Valyria.

00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:26.225
When I return with wagons spilling over with silks and silver,

00:52:26.226 --> 00:52:28.145
Who will be the first...

00:52:29.480 --> 00:52:31.981
...to celebrate in the spoils of conquest?

00:52:31.982 --> 00:52:33.233
We will!

00:52:34.360 --> 00:52:35.943
Groups of three and four!

00:52:35.944 --> 00:52:38.071
No man walks alone.

00:52:38.072 --> 00:52:41.492
Woodgard, Owtram, you oversee the market square.

00:52:44.411 --> 00:52:47.664
It seems the Lord of Flea Bottom has not been altogether forgotten.

00:52:47.665 --> 00:52:49.874
We've apprehended someone, Your Grace.

00:52:49.875 --> 00:52:51.210
At River Row.

00:52:51.835 --> 00:52:53.796
Then he will be the first to be repaid.

00:52:56.006 --> 00:52:57.799
Fall in!

00:52:57.800 --> 00:52:59.760
Stoney Sept beyond the rise!

00:53:21.865 --> 00:53:23.283
What is it?

00:53:26.495 --> 00:53:28.122
The Rivermen have crossed.

00:53:29.623 --> 00:53:31.250
And burned the bridge behind them.

00:53:33.127 --> 00:53:35.713
We can no longer delay their march.

00:53:40.884 --> 00:53:42.219
So we failed.

00:54:17.963 --> 00:54:19.338
How many others?

00:54:19.339 --> 00:54:21.008
Who was with you?

00:54:24.803 --> 00:54:27.139
I was the only one. I swear it.

00:54:28.182 --> 00:54:31.184
- I acted alone. - Under whose instruction?

00:54:31.185 --> 00:54:33.519
I never saw his face, I told you.

00:54:33.520 --> 00:54:34.980
The tongue or the eye?

00:54:38.942 --> 00:54:39.860
The eye.

00:54:41.361 --> 00:54:44.239
It was the king, he said! Please!

00:54:46.200 --> 00:54:48.534
He said it was the king's work I was to be about.

00:54:48.535 --> 00:54:49.870
It was Aegon then.

00:54:51.872 --> 00:54:53.081
No.

00:54:54.833 --> 00:54:56.376
Look.

00:54:58.670 --> 00:55:00.172
In my boot.

00:55:05.093 --> 00:55:07.971
Compliments of King Daeron Targaryen, he said.

00:55:09.097 --> 00:55:11.892
For killing traitors to his throne.

00:55:20.442 --> 00:55:23.529
No! No! Please!

00:55:28.534 --> 00:55:30.493
There's none who may say that you did not give

00:55:30.494 --> 00:55:32.203
Your best effort.

00:55:32.204 --> 00:55:36.083
Perhaps this is the best we could have hoped for.

00:55:37.084 --> 00:55:41.129
We've made our mark and returned alive...

00:55:42.923 --> 00:55:44.424
...to Tumbleton, perhaps...

00:55:45.926 --> 00:55:47.928
To find out what Ormund has planned.

00:55:50.556 --> 00:55:52.724
I thank you for your offer, Ser Gwayne.

00:55:54.977 --> 00:55:56.645
But my path is set before me.

00:55:58.647 --> 00:56:00.606
And what is...

00:56:00.607 --> 00:56:01.984
What is that path?

00:56:03.569 --> 00:56:05.195
We'll raft the river.

00:56:06.196 --> 00:56:07.656
Or swim it.

00:56:09.283 --> 00:56:11.660
It was one thing to obstruct them, Ser Criston, but...

00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:15.664
You must see they've gained the advantage.

00:56:17.249 --> 00:56:18.583
What more can we do?

00:56:18.584 --> 00:56:20.252
We will join them...

00:56:21.336 --> 00:56:22.754
In battle.

00:56:23.755 --> 00:56:25.840
Face them head on.

00:56:25.841 --> 00:56:27.926
We have half the men that we set out with.

00:56:29.469 --> 00:56:31.722
There are 200 Rivermen for every one of us.

00:56:32.764 --> 00:56:34.516
That-- you...

00:56:35.267 --> 00:56:37.185
It would march us towards certain death.

00:56:52.159 --> 00:56:55.203
This was your goal, wasn't it?

00:56:56.580 --> 00:56:57.789
All along.

00:56:58.624 --> 00:57:00.792
Our fate was always assured, Ser Gwayne.

00:57:03.170 --> 00:57:05.088
When we set out, we were doomed...

00:57:06.048 --> 00:57:08.090
To death and defeat.

00:57:08.091 --> 00:57:10.677
I have offered you sanctuary.

00:57:11.845 --> 00:57:13.387
Or at least the hope of one.

00:57:13.388 --> 00:57:15.349
You have offered me service to your house.

00:57:17.935 --> 00:57:19.561
I am grateful.

00:57:22.356 --> 00:57:24.733
But I have been a servant all my life.

00:57:27.402 --> 00:57:28.987
To green or to black.

00:57:31.198 --> 00:57:33.492
I have defined myself by oaths...

00:57:34.910 --> 00:57:36.411
Through unyielding devotion.

00:57:37.955 --> 00:57:40.999
And the highborn have made much of me while it pleased them to do so.

00:57:45.212 --> 00:57:47.297
But I will not let them diminish me now.

00:57:50.550 --> 00:57:53.720
I will not return spurned...

00:57:55.347 --> 00:57:56.723
Rejected.

00:57:59.351 --> 00:58:01.436
I am the realm's greatest warrior.

00:58:04.022 --> 00:58:05.691
And I will die as such.

00:58:08.026 --> 00:58:09.194
Clear-eyed.

00:58:10.612 --> 00:58:11.697
Unbent.

00:58:13.490 --> 00:58:14.908
Glorious in battle.

00:58:17.160 --> 00:58:20.122
And not in their service, finally.

00:58:22.165 --> 00:58:23.375
But in my own.

00:58:28.088 --> 00:58:29.881
And they will sing songs of it.

00:58:36.013 --> 00:58:38.056
And Queen Alicent herself will hear them.

00:58:46.606 --> 00:58:49.650
The plan is to rebuild the fleet at Driftmark,

00:58:49.651 --> 00:58:51.652
But it will take time.

00:58:51.653 --> 00:58:53.447
The Velaryon resources are diminished.

00:58:54.573 --> 00:58:57.199
A condition with which I am all too familiar.

00:58:57.200 --> 00:58:58.827
The king consort, Your Grace.

00:59:00.495 --> 00:59:01.997
My prince.

00:59:04.791 --> 00:59:06.752
The price of our humiliation.

00:59:10.005 --> 00:59:11.965
- What is this? - Who is this.

00:59:13.383 --> 00:59:15.634
Young Daeron Targaryen.

00:59:15.635 --> 00:59:17.804
Ormund has declared him king.

00:59:20.265 --> 00:59:22.142
We should have burned them when we had the chance.

00:59:32.402 --> 00:59:34.528
<i>We have endured much.</i>

00:59:34.529 --> 00:59:36.656
Suffered much.

00:59:37.616 --> 00:59:39.242
This I know.

00:59:41.578 --> 00:59:44.372
And though we languish now...

00:59:45.499 --> 00:59:46.750
In the darkness...

00:59:48.794 --> 00:59:50.712
We will not lose heart.

00:59:52.297 --> 00:59:53.965
Come to bed.

00:59:55.550 --> 00:59:56.927
She hears something.

01:00:02.891 --> 01:00:05.060
<i>The Seven watch over us even now.</i>

01:00:11.691 --> 01:00:13.151
Look.

01:00:19.699 --> 01:00:21.409
<i>Let the Maiden grant us vision.</i>

01:00:22.786 --> 01:00:24.621
<i>For the way ahead is blessed.</i>

01:00:32.671 --> 01:00:35.132
Let the Warrior lend us his sword

01:00:38.593 --> 01:00:40.595
That we do not falter in our resolve.

01:00:42.305 --> 01:00:43.890
And the Smith...

01:00:46.726 --> 01:00:48.061
Let's go.

01:00:49.604 --> 01:00:52.149
Let the Smith bless us with his strength.

01:00:54.818 --> 01:00:56.903
<i>The Crone lights our way.</i>

01:00:59.281 --> 01:01:01.741
<i>Ours is the path of righteousness.</i>

01:01:05.871 --> 01:01:06.955
Ser Luthor?

01:01:13.128 --> 01:01:14.712
Careful.

01:01:14.713 --> 01:01:16.506
<i>The Mother gives her comfort.</i>

01:01:17.674 --> 01:01:19.384
<i>The Father, his protection.</i>

01:01:20.802 --> 01:01:23.346
No. No, it's blocked.

01:01:24.472 --> 01:01:25.681
We have to go back.

01:01:25.682 --> 01:01:28.018
There is no way back, the door is shut!

01:01:35.066 --> 01:01:37.194
No, no, no, no, no! No!

01:01:40.155 --> 01:01:41.698
<i>And the Stranger...</i>

01:02:02.219 --> 01:02:04.387
<i>The Stranger offers us rest.</i>

